## 5. Fonts — drop-in contract

User provides the files. **Place them here:**

```
frontend/src/assets/fonts/
  KohinoorTelugu-Regular.(otf|ttf)      ← body  (Medium/Bold optional but nice)
  KohinoorTelugu-Medium.(otf|ttf)
  KohinoorTelugu-Bold.(otf|ttf)
  SmileySans-Bold.(otf|ttf|woff2)       ← accent (得意黑 / Smiley Sans Oblique works too)
  BehanceDXBurst.(otf|ttf)              ← burst  (the graffiti tag face)
```

Wiring: `next/font/local` in `src/app/layout.tsx`, exposing
`--font-body`, `--font-accent`, `--font-burst`, mapped in `globals.css @theme`.
Smiley Sans is open-source (SIL/its own license) and can be self-hosted; if the user
prefers, we fetch it ourselves. Kohinoor Telugu + DX Burst must come from the user.

Until files land, the build falls back: body → humanist sans stack, accent → heavy
grotesque, burst → a bold display fallback, so layout is testable before fonts arrive.

