## 7. Build status & font swap (as of 2026-06-08)

**Built:** every screen + shared chrome, black-base poster aesthetic, copy rewritten.
`next build` passes (9 routes). All work is in `Feature-FasterRecommendations` branch,
uncommitted.

**Fonts currently wired (in `layout.tsx`):**
| Role | var | Currently | Status |
|---|---|---|---|
| accent | `--font-accent` | **Smiley Sans** (self-hosted `src/assets/fonts/SmileySans-Oblique.woff2`) | ✅ final |
| body | `--font-body` | **Hind** (next/font/google) | ⏳ SUBSTITUTE for Kohinoor Telugu |
| burst | `--font-burst` | **Permanent Marker** (next/font/google) | ⏳ SUBSTITUTE for behance DX Burst |

**To swap a substitute for the real file:**
1. Drop the file in `src/assets/fonts/` (e.g. `KohinoorTelugu-Regular.woff2`,
   `BehanceDXBurst.woff2`).
2. In `layout.tsx`, replace the matching `next/font/google` import with a
   `localFont({ src: "../assets/fonts/<file>", variable: "--font-body" | "--font-burst" })`.
3. Remove the now-unused google import. Nothing in globals.css/components changes —
   they only reference the CSS variables.

The `.tag` / `.tag-flat` graffiti treatment lives in `globals.css`; once real DX Burst
lands it will look markedly more "spray tag" than the Permanent Marker placeholder.

